<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How domains are counted</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Each production domain where the plan key is saved uses one domain slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local and staging sites do not use a slot. By default, up to 3 of them can be active on one key at the same time.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local sites include <code>localhost</code>, private IP addresses and addresses ending in <code>.local</code> or <code>.test</code>. Staging sites include subdomains such as <code>staging.</code>, <code>dev.</code> or <code>test.</code> and common hosting staging domains.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>You can remove a domain in your wopcart.com account to free its slot and use the key on another site.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Removing the plan key from a site's settings also releases that site's slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"backgroundColor":"accent-5","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
